WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:04.310
<b>To the Sea</b>

38
00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.870
That crazy rubber guy
beat Captain Kuro!

39
00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.240
[PIRATE I] Not even the marines
were a match for Kuro,

40
00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.250
Man of a Thousand Plans!
And this guy still beat him!

41
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.250
[PIRATE A] Just...
just who are you?!

42
00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:26.630
I'm Monkey D. Luffy.

43
00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:31.630
The only time a pirate should abandon
his name is when he dies!

44
00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.630
I would never lose to a coward
who ditches his name,

45
00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.550
betrays his friends,
and runs from life on the sea.

46
00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:40.930
Uh... Luffy... I never heard
that name before.

47
00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.440
You should remember my name
for the rest of your lives.

48
00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.150
'Cause one of these days I'm
gonna be King of the Pirates!

49
00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:49.650
[PIRATES murmur]

50
00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.690
You are?

51
00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:55.450
Now get outta here!

52
00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.070
[PIRATES gasping]

53
00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:59.200
And never come back!

54
00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.990
[PIRATES chatter]

55
00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.410
[NAMI panting]

56
00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.260
Ya did good, Luffy.

57
00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:19.800
[NAMI] I'd expect even you to collapse
after what you just went through. Say...

58
00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.890
Tell me, why were you
so mad earlier?

59
00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.480
'Cause I truly hate people

60
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.570
That is not how
friends should act.

61
00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.400
[NAMI] What
are you talking about?

62
00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.950
Of course it isn't.
Most pirates aren't the brave,

63
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.410
honorable people you always
make out them to be.

64
00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:41.780
I want some meat.

65
00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.500
– [NAMI] You're unbelievable!
– [LUFFY groaning]

66
00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:55.510
[USOPP] Hey, guys, think you can keep
everything that just happened here secret?

67
00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.180
What? A secret!

68
00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.090
Why would we want
to keep all this a secret?!

69
00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.340
Yeah! Why, huh?

70
00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.810
We put our lives on the line
to save the village!

71
00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:05.480
Now everyone'll change
their opinion of you so

72
00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:08.810
instead of being Usopp the liar,
you'll be Usopp the hero!

73
00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.350
[CHILDREN cheering]

74
00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.480
Really, Usopp...

75
00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.690
You need to clear up
this misunderstanding.

76
00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.650
Misunderstanding...?
I was known as the village liar

77
00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:20.490
because I lied
all the time, Miss Kaya.

78
00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.530
They were right
to not believe me.

79
00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:26.540
Besides, there's no point in scaring people
with something that's already over.

80
00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:29.330
And I seriously doubt
that any more pirates like Kuro

81
00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.000
and his gang will show up.
There's no reason for pirates

82
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.550
to attack our out-of-the-way,
little village.

83
00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.630
So listen up! Pretend
this never happened! 'Kay?

84
00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:42.680
This was all just another one
of my great, big lies.

85
00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.890
Now I won't force
you to, but...

86
00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:52.150
No, I can do it! I'll do whatever it takes
for the good of the village, Captain!

87
00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:53.230
Yeah, me too!

88
00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.070
Me, too. My lips
are totally sealed, I promise!

89
00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:57.110
[CHILDREN chattering]

90
00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:00.780
Kaya... Will you...
Will you tell?

91
00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:04.990
[KAYA] No.

92
00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.290
Something just isn't
right this morning.

93
00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:13.380
Where is Usopp?

94
00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.960
It kinda throws everything off
if he's not around.

95
00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.090
I feel so bored.

96
00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:20.220
[LITTLE GIRL] Mama!

97
00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:23.680
Is that screaming liar guy
not coming to town today?

98
00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.970
[MAN] That lying little twerp!

99
00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.600
Where the heck is he?

100
00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:31.850
You don't think I hurt
his feelings yesterday, do you?

101
00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.060
Oh, don't worry.

102
00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.900
He'll be up to his old tricks in no time.

103
00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.400
[MAN] I hope so.

104
00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:42.700
[USOPP laughs] Thanks, guys!

105
00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:46.030
I wouldn't have been able
to protect the village without you.

106
00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.580
Give credit where credit's due.

107
00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:52.330
If you'd just stood by and done nothing,
I wouldn't have done anything, either.

108
00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.170
Yeah! Same here!

109
00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:55.500
Who cares about any of that?

110
00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.340
I've got my hands
on this sweet, sweet treasure now.

111
00:05:58.340 --> 00:05:59.510
And I couldn't be happier.

112
00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:01.590
[USOPP laughs]

113
00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.180
Everything that happened
here today helped me.

114
00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.310
I've just come to a very
difficult decision...

115
00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:09.460
[LUFFY] Uh?!

116
00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.730
[CARROT] Captain Usopp! What
did you want to talk to us about?

117
00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:24.110
[USOPP] The three of you fought well
against those terrible Black Cat Pirates.

118
00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:27.700
As Captain, I'm proud of you
for being so brave and courageous.

119
00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:31.660
Thanks to you, we overcame
our biggest and most important

120
00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.370
battle since we formed
the Usopp Pirates five years ago.

121
00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.590
That was when you three brave soldiers
were only four years old. Remember?

122
00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:38.380
[CHILDREN] Yep!

123
00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.840
Now I know this is
sudden, but...

124
00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:43.670
I've decided that I'm gonna
set out to sea by myself.

125
00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:49.220
I'm finally gonna leave this place
and become a real pirate!

126
00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:56.770
At first, I wasn't sure
what I would do.

127
00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:00.150
I couldn't decide if I wanted
to stay here forever or not.

128
00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:03.780
But once I saw them, I knew deep
in my heart what I must do.

129
00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:08.910
I feel that, as a man,
I must set out to the vast ocean. So...

130
00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.330
– I'm leaving this place behind!
– [PEPPER, ONION, CARROT] Uh?

131
00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:16.670
I leave for one reason!
When the great pirate flag beckons,

132
00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:20.090
you must heed its call!

133
00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.470
[CARROT] Captain!
Say it isn't so!

134
00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:26.260
[PEPPER, ONION, CARROT panting]

135
00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:27.930
You're lying again, right?!

136
00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:31.010
Isn't that a bit hasty?!
There's no reason to leave!

137
00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:32.810
I thought you loved
this village!

138
00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:37.850
And what's gonna happen
to the Usopp Pirates without you?

139
00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:40.480
[USOPP] You've been
so good to me, guys.

140
00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.990
I plan to leave
without telling the villagers.

141
00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:45.990
Give them my regards.

142
00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.240
Captain...

143
00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:49.120
No, I don't want to!

144
00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.990
Don't go, Captain!
Just stay here! Please.

145
00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.960
Usopp Pirates.
Do you remember this place?

146
00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.580
This is where we first met,
and formed the Usopp Pirates.

147
00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:09.510
[laughing] Finished!

148
00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.430
[CARROT] Hey, it's
that liar guy!

149
00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:13.140
[USOPP] Huh?
Who are you guys?

150
00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:14.770
And why are you
so buddy-buddy with me?

151
00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:16.390
Well, duh! You're famous!

152
00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:19.150
Yeah. You're
a really famous guy!

153
00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.560
Right! I know,
you've come face to face

154
00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.190
with the man that is known
the world over as Captain Usopp!

155
00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.700
Actually, everyone in the village
calls you Liar Usopp.

156
00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:28.950
[PEPPER, ONION laugh]

157
00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:29.910
[USOPP] Ah!

158
00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:33.910
'Kay! From this day forth, you're
officially members of the Usopp Pirates!

159
00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:34.950
[ALL] Huh?

160
00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:37.000
C'mon! Man up!

161
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.380
[whimpers] A lot's happened
since then, huh?

162
00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:41.960
[dog barks]

163
00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:45.800
[USOPP] A Cerberus!
Scare it away!

164
00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.880
A dragon! Capture it!

165
00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.970
Flour Star!

166
00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:54.260
[PEPPER] You're
amazing, Captain!

167
00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:58.680
[USOPP] But of course! I'm
a brave warrior of the sea!

168
00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:55.890
– [USOPP laughs]
– [CHILDREN sigh]

169
00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.690
Please don't talk about the
old days! I can't stand it!

170
00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.980
Pepper's right!
It's much too painful.

171
00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.780
This kind of lie isn't like you,
Captain! It's not fun.

172
00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.400
Why would you say
that you're going to leave us?

173
00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.570
[CARROT] You're not
serious, are you?

174
00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.660
[ONION] You're being stupid,
Captain! Stupid!

175
00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:20.410
[CHILDREN cry]

176
00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:27.340
Alright, men! Tell me
what all your ambitions are!

177
00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:30.470
When I grow up my dream
is... to run a pub!

178
00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:33.220
My whole life I've wanted
to be a master carpenter!

179
00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:35.390
My goal is to become a writer!

180
00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:38.020
Then, swear to me now
that each of you

181
00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:41.310
will continue on your paths!
Promise me that you will never

182
00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:45.310
let the fires
of your ambitions die out!

183
00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.980
[USOPP] As of today...

184
00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.280
our group...

185
00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:51.700
the Usopp Pirates... [cries]

186
00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:02.620
[USOPP] are disbanded!

187
00:10:07.550 --> 00:10:10.300
Now that we've eaten,
we should probably get going.

188
00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:11.630
Yeah, you're right.

189
00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:14.510
[KAYA] Here you are!

190
00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:15.890
Hello there, Miss!

191
00:10:15.890 --> 00:10:17.510
Are you all right
being out of bed?

192
00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.520
[KAYA] Yes.

193
00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:22.270
I think now I can
truly start recovering.

194
00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:24.230
You see, my sickness
this last year was caused

195
00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:27.020
by the mental shock of losing
both my parents.

196
00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:30.150
And Usopp's friendship
helped me start getting better.

197
00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:32.780
I can't stay in bed
forever, you know.

198
00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:37.660
I've prepared a present for you
from the bottom of my heart

199
00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:41.080
to show you how grateful I am
for everything you've done here.

200
00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.580
I'd be honored
if you'd accept it.

201
00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.670
[sighs] All packed!

202
00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:54.090
[USOPP] Guess it's farewell
to this house, too.

203
00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:00.000
[USOPP]
Hey!

204
00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:09.060
[USOPP grunting] I
can't get out!

205
00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:12.530
This stupid backpack!

206
00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:15.610
[USOPP grunting]

207
00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:32.630
A real caravel!

208
00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:36.880
[LUFFY] Are you actually
giving this to us?!

209
00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.800
[KAYA] Mm-hm. As a token
of my appreciation.

210
00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:42.640
[MERRY] It's
a slightly older model,

211
00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:46.480
but I personally designed
it and she sails like a dream.

212
00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:51.270
She has a carvel-make caravel with
lateen sails and a central stern rudder.

213
00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.030
She's a fine ship,
and her name is the Going Merry.

214
00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:58.950
[MERRY] Allow
me to explain the rigging.

215
00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:02.030
First, about the Kruger net yard
adjustment, it may seem a little...

216
00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:05.410
Hold on! You'd be better off just
explaining the technical stuff to me!

217
00:12:06.460 --> 00:12:09.380
[LUFFY] What a cool ship!
Have you guys seen the front?

218
00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:12.130
It's totally awesome!

219
00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:15.840
We've loaded it with all the provisions
you might need on a long voyage.

220
00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:18.630
[LUFFY] Thanks! It leaves
nothing to beat tired!

221
00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:21.180
That's "leaves nothing
to be desired", idiot.

222
00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.060
[USOPP yelping]

223
00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:24.640
[ALL] Uh?!

224
00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:26.890
Oh, no, Usopp!

225
00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:30.730
Hey, what's
he doing? Looks fun.

226
00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:32.610
Well, we'd better stop him.

227
00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.780
That weirdo, is on a collision
course with our boat.

228
00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.860
Uh. Hey, thanks, guys.

229
00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.490
Anytime.

230
00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.330
[KAYA] You're really doing it.

231
00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:45.910
You're gonna take
to the ocean.

232
00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.200
[USOPP] Yeah.

233
00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:51.380
I've decided to get going
before I have time to change my mind.

234
00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:53.540
[USOPP] Please,
don't stop me.

235
00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:56.460
[KAYA] I won't. I know
it's time for you to go.

236
00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:59.510
Kaya, don't be sad about it.

237
00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:01.760
Just think, the next time
I come back here,

238
00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:05.350
I'll tell you about adventures that'll
sound more like lies than my old lies.

239
00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:09.140
Good. I'll look forward to it.

240
00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:11.690
[USOPP] You guys take care!
I hope we meet again sometime!

241
00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:14.820
How come?!

242
00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.650
Uh. Well... Because I...

243
00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.820
Are you antisocial
or something...?

244
00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:20.900
I'm taking off for life
on the high seas,

245
00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:23.820
and I hope that we'll eventually
meet again, that's all.

246
00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:25.580
What are you talkin' about?

247
00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:26.450
Get on already!

248
00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.330
Huh?!

249
00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.790
We're friends.
Right? So get on.

250
00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:34.380
[USOPP] This is it...

251
00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.130
I'm really a Pirate Captain now!

252
00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.760
[LUFFY] Don't be stupid,
Usopp! I'm the Captain!

253
00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:42.510
[ZORO, NAMI, LUFFY laugh]

254
00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.550
[USOPP laughs]

255
00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.970
[ALL laughing]

256
00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.620
[CARROT] There goes
the Captain...

257
00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:08.040
[PEPPER] He fell in with some pretty awesome
people, so I'm not too worried.

258
00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.790
[ONION] Yeah,
he'll be safe with them.

259
00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:12.920
I've never seen
anybody as strong as they are.

260
00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:15.080
He's always talked
about becoming a pirate,

261
00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.790
and now he's headed off
to live his dreams!

262
00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:20.050
You know the villagers are gonna be
sad when we break the news to 'em.

263
00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:23.760
Our Captain was the only person
who could liven things up around here.

264
00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:26.430
And now he's gone.

265
00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:28.850
[ONION, CARROT] What is it?

266
00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:30.430
Hey! I just had a great idea!

267
00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:33.140
[MERRY] They certainly were
a pleasant bunch.

268
00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:34.140
[KAYA] Merry...

269
00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.560
[MERRY] Yes?

270
00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.940
[KAYA] Lying hurts... A lot.

271
00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:41.650
[MERRY] Are you referring
to Klahadore?

272
00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.530
[KAYA] No.

273
00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:45.860
You must be talking
about Usopp.

274
00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.910
You really wanted
him to stay, didn't you?

275
00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:56.250
Miss Kaya. Years ago, one
of the villagers told me a story

276
00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:59.210
about your good friend
Usopp's childhood.

277
00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:04.220
Only a short time after his father
left the village to become a pirate.

278
00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:07.260
His mother, whom he was
very close to, passed away.

279
00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:09.010
[KAYA] Uh?

280
00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:14.140
[USOPP] Pirates!
Pirates are here!

281
00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:15.890
[USOPP panting] Pirates are here!

282
00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.480
Dad's pirates are here
Mom! They're here!

283
00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:21.110
Hold on, Usopp, you
mustn't shout! Calm down!

284
00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:25.950
Mom, we're saved! Dad
finally came back for us!

285
00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:29.870
Uh. There you go with
your wild imagination again.

286
00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:31.240
You silly boy.

287
00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.830
It's true. He always said
he'd come back for us

288
00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:37.250
and take us with him
when you got better, didn't he Mom?

289
00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:38.580
Usopp, my dear.

290
00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.420
Your father
won't be coming back.

291
00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:48.640
But... I'm proud to have married
such a brave man who dared to chase his dreams.

292
00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:50.640
I heard about a special medicine...

293
00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:52.930
This stuff can cure
any sickness!

294
00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:57.020
So silly. You dream too much.

295
00:15:57.020 --> 00:16:02.150
I am a dreamer! And I'm silly!
It's true. I'm proud of it!

296
00:16:02.150 --> 00:16:05.400
After all, I'm
the son of a pirate!

297
00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.570
Promise me one thing.

298
00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:11.490
Promise me you'll grow up
to be brave, like him.

299
00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:22.000
[USOPP] Pirates are coming!

300
00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.880
[MERRY] Perhaps out
of loneliness.

301
00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:27.510
He continued to shout it
after his mother passed away.

302
00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:30.260
In the hopes that one day
his father's pirate ship

303
00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:34.060
would be at the shore, ready
to spirit him away to the sea,

304
00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:37.270
and give him a family
that he never had.

305
00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:46.070
[MERRY] The villagers say that his outlandish lies
contain his most heartfelt wish.

306
00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:49.700
[USOPP] Pirates!
Pirates are coming!

307
00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:54.620
[MERRY] As someone else who lost
both parents, he saw you as a kindred spirit,

308
00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:58.000
and he couldn't sit by
and ignore your suffering.

309
00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:03.170
Now it's time for you too
to rise from the ashes of tragedy.

310
00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:06.880
And live up to the example
that Usopp worked so hard to set.

311
00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.590
Yes!

312
00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.640
[LUFFY] Cheers to a new ship
and a new crewmate!

313
00:17:17.270 --> 00:17:19.640
[ALL laughing, cheering]

314
00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:24.650
[KAYA] They said
that they were fighting to live.

315
00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:26.280
Not to die.

316
00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:33.320
Usopp's wild stories and outlandish lies
always spoke of the joy of being alive.

317
00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.990
They helped me through my grief by
cheering me up and telling me to live!

318
00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:38.080
[MERRY] Indeed!

319
00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.580
Okay!

320
00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:40.790
We're really doing this?

321
00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:41.580
[ONION] Mm-hm.

322
00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:42.830
You bet!

323
00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.170
We're gonna follow
in our great Captain's footsteps!

324
00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:50.010
[ALL inhale]

325
00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:53.470
[ALL] Pirates!
Pirates are coming!

326
00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:54.800
Pirates! Run for your lives!

327
00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:58.930
[KAYA] My life starts now,
Merry. I'm going to be a doctor.

328
00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:03.350
[MERRY] That's wonderful,
Miss Kaya. Just wonderful.

329
00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:14.180
As a kid I had a dream of a dazzling treasure

330
00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:21.200
I had a map in my head that I knew would lead me

331
00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:28.300
Charted a course all on my own so nobody would beat me

332
00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:35.560
The promised land was in my hand drew a line in the sand

333
00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.940
Look where I am

334
00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:49.350
My one ambitions slipping right through my hands

335
00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:56.620
But if the world ever changes Ill call out your name

336
00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:03.700
We could return to a time when our lives were still the same

337
00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:10.830
Take me to the place where memories remain

338
00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:16.700
Please dont ever let them fade
